Hold the last frame while the shell redraws a prompt a resize erased.

A resize erases the prompt line (Screen.clearPromptForRedraw) for the shell to
redraw, and the renderer showed the erased grid until the shell answered
SIGWINCH, so the prompt line blinked on every resize: with a shell answering
150 ms late, libghostty-spm measured 398 of 1201 frames with no prompt, 0 with
this. The erase stays, so reflow leaves no stale prompt. The renderer keeps
its last frame until OSC 133 B and the erased input are back, a command starts
(133 C), a full reset, or a deadline it sets itself from the first held frame.

From libghostty-spm's Patches/ghostty/0015-hold-frame-for-prompt-redraw.sh (MIT, 2026 @Lakr233),
cut as a `git diff` against the ThirdParty/ghostty pin.

